.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_SIGN 3 2026-09-18 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_sign \- configure weak signing before writer close
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_sign("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "archive,"
.BI "        uint32_t " "signature_type,"
.BI "        const uint8_t *" "private_key,"
.BI "        size_t " "private_key_size"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configures \fIarchive\fP, an active MPQ v1 or v2 writer, to generate one
\fIsignature_type\fP: \fBLIBMPQ_SIGNATURE_WEAK\fP or
\fBLIBMPQ_SIGNATURE_STRONG\fP. A file writer must not be active. Each
type may be configured once; ordinary MPQ archives may use both.
Configuration is non-consuming and copies the caller's
\fIprivate_key\fP. Final signing occurs when
\fBlibmpq__archive_close\fP(3) finalizes the archive; reopen it to
inspect or verify the result.
.PP
Weak private keys are exactly 128 raw bytes: a 64-byte unsigned
big-endian modulus and a zero-padded 64-byte private exponent. Strong
private keys have the same layout with 256-byte fields, 512 bytes total.
The modulus must be full-width and odd; the exponent must be odd, at
least 3, and less than the modulus. The checks validate representation,
not mathematical key-pair validity. No PEM parser or default or
product-specific keys are built in.
.PP
Weak signing creates an internal \fB(signature)\fP member and consumes a
file slot. Strong signing appends an external NGIS trailer using the plain
SHA-1 archive-range variant. MPQE writers support internal weak signing
but reject external strong signing because no MPQE transport
representation is defined for it. Both algorithms are legacy
compatibility mechanisms, not modern trust primitives.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP after configuration, or a negative libmpq
error. A failed request does not consume the writer handle.
.SH ERRORS
NULL archive handles return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST\fP; invalid type,
key, duplicate configuration, or MPQE strong signing return
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT\fP. Wrong writer state returns
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP. Allocation and capacity errors may
also propagate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_signatures (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_verify (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_sign (3)
